# Infrastructure and database safety

## No infrastructure restarts

NEVER restart, stop, recreate, or otherwise disrupt running infrastructure unless the user explicitly directs it in the current message.

Forbidden without explicit user direction:
- `docker restart`, `docker stop`, `docker compose restart/down/up` (or equivalents)
- Restarting Temporal workers, orchestrators, go-executor, web, db, redis, neo4j, proxy, MCP, or any other stack service
- Killing processes that belong to the running stack
- Any “to pick up the change” restart of containers/services

Code/file edits on mounted volumes are fine. If a restart is needed for a change to take effect, tell the user — do not perform it.

## No manual database schema changes

NEVER alter the database schema manually (raw SQL DDL, `psql`, Django shell hacks, direct table/column edits, etc.) unless the user explicitly says otherwise in the current message.

Schema changes MUST go through Django migrations:
- Create/update migration files
- Apply with `migrate` (only when the user asks you to run migrations)

Do not use `migrate --run-syncdb`, fake-apply, or hand-edit live schema as a shortcut.
